WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.004 --> 00:00:16.564
noticed that the storm had stopped long ago.

2
00:00:17.265 --> 00:00:19.445
He told the doctor that he should go home.

3
00:00:19.465 --> 00:00:22.846
"You have to eat something," insisted Dr.

4
00:00:22.886 --> 00:00:25.907
Dolittle. "It's a long walk back to your house."

5
00:00:27.047 --> 00:00:28.568
So Tommy stayed for dinner.

6
00:00:29.788 --> 00:00:33.410
During the meal, Polynesia explained why she had returned.

7
00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:36.851
"I miss the adventure and excitement!"

8
00:00:37.431 --> 00:00:37.931
she said.

9
00:00:37.951 --> 00:00:43.674
"I will always love Africa, but I miss going on voyages with you, Doctor."

10
00:00:43.694 --> 00:00:48.436
"Will you be going on another voyage soon, Dr.

11
00:00:48.476 --> 00:00:50.097
Dolittle?" asked Tommy.

12
00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:53.118
The doctor pushed away his empty plate.

13
00:00:53.138 --> 00:00:57.300
"Well, I must say, I've been thinking about he began.

14
00:00:58.716 --> 00:01:03.159
But before he had a chance to answer, an owl flew into the room.

15
00:01:03.179 --> 00:01:08.902
"Oh, hello, Too-Too," the doctor said in greeting.

16
00:01:08.922 --> 00:01:10.482
"You're up early!"

17
00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.303
"Welcome home, Dr.

18
00:01:12.323 --> 00:01:14.225
Dolittle!" the owl hooted.

19
00:01:14.965 --> 00:01:16.946
Dr. Dolittle ran to the window.

20
00:01:16.966 --> 00:01:18.567
"Oh, dear!

21
00:01:18.967 --> 00:01:20.668
Tommy, we'd better get going.

22
00:01:21.108 --> 00:01:22.729
It's already dark outside."

23
00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:26.511
"I'll come with you," said Polynesia.

24
00:01:28.272 --> 00:01:31.713
It was very late when they finally arrived at Tommy's house.

25
00:01:32.773 --> 00:01:35.134
His mother was quite worried and upset.

26
00:01:35.154 --> 00:01:37.155
"It's my fault, Mrs.

27
00:01:37.195 --> 00:01:39.295
Stubbins," apologized Dr.

28
00:01:39.335 --> 00:01:44.197
Dolittle. Tommy's mother stared at the little man with the parrot on his shoulder.

29
00:01:44.217 --> 00:01:47.017
"And who might you be, sir?"

30
00:01:47.578 --> 00:01:48.118
she asked.

31
00:01:50.238 --> 00:01:52.219
Dr. Dolittle introduced himself.

32
00:01:52.859 --> 00:01:55.980
Then he stuck out his foot and pointed to his boots.

33
00:01:56.744 --> 00:02:00.687
"These were made by your husband, a very fine shoemaker indeed."

34
00:02:01.367 --> 00:02:02.688
Tommy's father blushed.

35
00:02:02.708 --> 00:02:04.169
"Thank you, sir.

36
00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:06.491
Won't you come in for some tea?"

37
00:02:06.891 --> 00:02:07.552
he invited.

38
00:02:07.572 --> 00:02:12.115
"Dr. Dolittle's come to look at the squirrel," said Tommy.

39
00:02:12.135 --> 00:02:16.918
"Tommy is always bringing home little animals," his mother said.

40
00:02:16.938 --> 00:02:21.401
"Perhaps he will grow up to be an animal doctor," the doctor exclaimed.

41
00:02:21.421 --> 00:02:25.324
"Doctor? Oh, no, sir," his father replied.

42
00:02:26.152 --> 00:02:28.313
"We don't have money to send Tommy to school."

43
00:02:29.274 --> 00:02:31.935
On hearing this, Tommy felt disappointed.

44
00:02:33.055 --> 00:02:35.897
Tommy took the doctor and Polynesia to his room.

45
00:02:36.717 --> 00:02:39.078
He tried not to show how upset he was.

46
00:02:39.839 --> 00:02:42.940
It was true—Tommy's family was very poor.

47
00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:45.901
They couldn't afford to send Tommy to school.

48
00:02:45.921 --> 00:02:49.043
"Here is the squirrel."

49
00:02:49.523 --> 00:02:50.984
Tommy held out the box.

50
00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:56.704
Dr. Dolittle peered inside and started making strange squeaky noises.

51
00:02:56.724 --> 00:03:00.687
"Hello, little friend," he was saying to the squirrel.

52
00:03:00.707 --> 00:03:03.310
"Oh, it's the great Dr.

53
00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:05.992
Dolittle," the squirrel said weakly.

54
00:03:06.012 --> 00:03:07.873
"Where does it hurt?"

55
00:03:08.334 --> 00:03:10.335
The doctor poked its leg gently.

56
00:03:12.457 --> 00:03:15.059
Tommy had wrapped the squirrel's leg in a bandage.

57
00:03:15.079 --> 00:03:19.002
"I thought his leg might be hurt," Tommy explained.

58
00:03:19.843 --> 00:03:20.764
The doctor nodded.

59
00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:22.581
"Yes, you did well.

60
00:03:22.921 --> 00:03:24.621
His leg is indeed hurt."

61
00:03:24.641 --> 00:03:29.844
"Tommy! Listen carefully to the squirrel," Polynesia instructed.

62
00:03:32.024 --> 00:03:35.806
Tommy bent down lower, but all he heard were squeaks.

63
00:03:35.826 --> 00:03:39.107
"I can't understand," he sighed.

64
00:03:39.127 --> 00:03:44.389
"Animal talk is more than just sounds," explained Polynesia.

65
00:03:44.409 --> 00:03:50.312
"Look at its gestures, its movements, and try to think like the squirrel."

66
00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:56.222
For the next few minutes, Tommy kept his eyes focused on the squirrel.

67
00:03:57.122 --> 00:04:01.504
Finally he jumped up and said: "He was attacked by a bird.

68
00:04:02.264 --> 00:04:03.805
He was hurt by a bird!"

69
00:04:03.825 --> 00:04:05.406
"Excellent, Tommy!

70
00:04:05.746 --> 00:04:06.486
And what else?"

71
00:04:07.066 --> 00:04:08.867
Polynesia said encouragingly.

72
00:04:09.627 --> 00:04:12.108
Tommy turned his attention back to the squirrel.

73
00:04:12.128 --> 00:04:16.230
"Well, uh," Tommy stammered.

74
00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:21.805
"The bird chased him up a tree, and then he found a delicious looking nut Dr.

75
00:04:21.845 --> 00:04:25.649
Dolittle and Polynesia looked at each other and tried not to laugh.

76
00:04:27.551 --> 00:04:30.133
"Not quite, Tommy," coughed Dr.

77
00:04:30.153 --> 00:04:33.256
Dolittle. "The bird took the squirrel's nut.

78
00:04:33.777 --> 00:04:35.899
But you were right about the bird attacking."

79
00:04:35.919 --> 00:04:42.626
"Doctor, I believe that Tommy may have the gift after all," Polynesia remarked.

80
00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:44.188
Tommy smiled.

81
00:04:46.128 --> 00:04:47.249
A little while later, Dr.

82
00:04:47.309 --> 00:04:51.111
Dolittle and Polynesia waved good-bye to their new friends.

83
00:04:51.131 --> 00:04:58.275
"I think one day Tommy could become an animal doctor like you," whispered Polynesia.

84
00:04:58.295 --> 00:05:00.957
"Yes," the doctor agreed.

85
00:05:00.977 --> 00:05:03.639
"I wonder what we can do to help him."
